90	 * when it was written and is not true now: Jira statuses ARE listable, through
91	 * the adapter's declared `list_project_statuses` capability. That correction
92	 * landed in `docs/setup-reference.md` and in `readStatuses` below, and this
93	 * comment one file away kept describing the world before it.
94	 *
95	 * Three states, deliberately distinguished, because collapsing them is how a
96	 * weaker claim gets laundered into a stronger one's wording:
97	 *   - `labels`              — genuinely unlistable; no Atlassian tool lists them.
98	 *   - `statuses`            — a full listing; plausibly complete, unprovably so.
99	 *   - `statuses:transitions`— derived from ONE issue's available transitions, so
100	 *     it is the set reachable from that issue's current state: PARTIAL BY
101	 *     CONSTRUCTION, not merely unproven. Row 4 refuses when the config lacks a
102	 *     status the listing names, so a shorter list is strictly EASIER to pass —
103	 *     which makes recording this distinctly a correctness matter and not
104	 *     bookkeeping.
105	 */
106	export type AssertedInput = "statuses" | "labels" | "statuses:transitions";
